This file notes the attributions and acknowledgments for the ReShade LumeniteFX project.

[ACKNOWLEDGMENT]
    For Lumenite's dense optical flow, pyramidal patch matching and optical flow
    fundamentals were studied from the following sources.

        1. AMD FidelityFX Optical Flow 1.1.2
           (https://gpuopen.com/manuals/fidelityfx_sdk/techniques/optical-flow/)
        2. Zenteon's (Daniel Oren-Ibarra) motion vectors (August 2025 version).
        3. Video++ (VPP) library's optical flow sources
           (https://github.com/matt-42/vpp/tree/master/vpp/algorithms/optical_flow)

    Also, a few ideas were borrowed from Zenteon such as the use of sparse samples for
    patch matching and that we should provide a disocclusion score alongside each motion
    vector. However, Lumenite's core flow technique is unique (based in continuous
    UV-space which requires its own specialized math, the specific use of previous
    frame flow and global motion direction, etc. without which its quality noticeably
    lacks), and its code/detailed implementation is original.

